  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the sum of pairwise outcome differences between lotteries, which involves comparing each outcome of one lottery to each outcome of the other. However, the individual’s deliberation centers on expected value computation, which is a different decision rule. The information considered by the individual (expected monetary value) does not match the information required by the decision reason (pairwise outcome differences). Furthermore, the justification—choosing based on higher expected gain—does not align with the rule of the decision reason, which would depend on aggregating outcome disparities. There is no indication in the verbal report of any attention to outcome differences or their summation. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
